          "**Meckel diverticulum** (2% of people, 2 feet from the ileocaecal valve) contains **ectopic gastric mucosa** that secretes acid and ulcerates adjacent ileum - the commonest cause of major painless rectal bleeding in a child. [Nelson 22e]",
          "**Coagulopathy in cirrhosis is rebalanced**, so a high INR does not predict bleeding - FFP adds volume and raises portal pressure without helping. [Baveno VII 2022]",
